        "text": {
          "type": "richtext",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>Yoto is a popular choice. These are the four differences that matter most when you compare it with Voxblock.</p><ul><li><strong>Price.</strong> The Yoto Mini (4th Gen) is £89.99 and the Yoto Player (4th Gen) is £119.99. The Voxblock player is £49.99.</li><li><strong>Setup.</strong> Yoto needs an app installed and wi-fi configured. Voxblock has no setup: put a book on the player and press play.</li><li><strong>Screens and data.</strong> Yoto players have a screen and log data. Voxblock has neither.</li><li><strong>The stories themselves.</strong> A Voxblock audiobook is a solid cardboard book with the story stored inside, made to sit on a shelf. A Yoto story is a slim card that downloads its audio over wi-fi.</li></ul>"
          }
        }
      },
